{
  "id": "COMPOUND:37050 - PROTEIN:6326",
  "verbalization": "Annoreticuin-9-One is implicated in the regulation of Phosphodiesterase 6C through multiple pathways, with the target entity Phosphodiesterase 6C being a common endpoint in several of its interactions. The evidence suggests that Annoreticuin-9-One acts as a target for multiple compounds, including CX-1, 8alpha,11-Elemodiol, and (5S)-5-[(2S)-1,2-dihydroxypropan-2-yl]-2-methylcyclohex-2-en-1-one, all of which are known to interact with Phosphodiesterase 6C. This indicates a potential mechanism by which Annoreticuin-9-One may influence the activity of Phosphodiesterase 6C, possibly through the modulation of downstream signaling pathways. The presence of multiple distinct targets that ultimately converge on Phosphodiesterase 6C suggests a complex regulatory network, where Annoreticuin-9-One may exert its effects through different molecular mechanisms. The integration of these pathways highlights the importance of Phosphodiesterase 6C in cellular processes, and the involvement of Annoreticuin-9-One in its regulation may provide a novel therapeutic avenue. The evidence supports a mechanistic link between Annoreticuin-9-One and Phosphodiesterase 6C, though further investigation is needed to elucidate the precise molecular interactions and functional roles.",
